INT. ROOFTOP PIGEON COOP - BROOKLYN - EVENING

A lopsided wooden coop on a tar roof. Wire mesh, birdseed, a hand-lettered sign reading "SQUAB SOCIAL CLUB - KEEP OFF." The skyline glows behind.

GUS PIZZUTI (60s, club president, bathrobe over trousers) holds a clipboard. His wife PAULETTE (60s, quilted vest) pours coffee from a thermos. Their nephew BARNABY (30s, sales rep, headset around his neck) stands stiffly in a suit that does not belong on a roof.

GUS
Tonight's race. Eight birds, three hundred yards, winner takes the pot.

BARNABY
Uncle Gus, I really need to take this call.

GUS
Everyone needs to take a call. Sit.

BARNABY
Is there a chair?

PAULETTE
There is an overturned bucket.

Barnaby sits on the bucket with the dignity of a man being sentenced. His headset buzzes. He holds up a finger and answers.

BARNABY
(into headset)
Barnaby Sinclair, how can I help you.

BOSS (V.O.)
Sinclair, where are you? The Henderson meeting started ten minutes ago.

BARNABY
I'm, uh, on a site visit.

BOSS (V.O.)
What site?

BARNABY
It's a, it's a coop.

BOSS (V.O.)
A what?

A pigeon lands on Barnaby's head. He freezes.

GUS
Don't move.

PAULETTE ^
Don't move.

BARNABY
(whispering, headset still live)
Please somebody take it.

BOSS (V.O.)
Sinclair! Is that a bird?

BARNABY
It's a client.
